	ZM 32:
	ZH 1:
	'　　　Leazas Castle'
	R
	ZM 24:
	ZH 1:
	R
	'　　　　　Audience Room'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Aristoles came at Rance’s'
	R
	'summons, and was respectfully'
	R
	'kneeling to him.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_0247d:
	ZH 1:
	'So?'
	R
	'Gotten used to the Leazas Army'
	R
	'yet?'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'Yes...'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_0247d:
	ZH 1:
	'What’s wrong?'
	R
	'Don’t space out in front of'
	R
	'the King.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'Ah... My apologies.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Uh...'
	R
	'I can never get Empress Sheila'
	R
	'completely off my mind.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_0247d:
	ZH 1:
	'Sheila?'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'Yes... I wonder whether me'
	R
	'having the right to say I love'
	R
	'her has any value...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'I had no idea about how'
	R
	'cruelly Stessel treated her.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_0247d:
	ZH 1:
	'Aah... So that’s what’s'
	R
	'bothering you?'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'...I want to go after him'
	R
	'right now and torture him'
	R
	'until he begs for death...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'King Rance, I’ll fight to meet'
	R
	'your expectations... So...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'If I’m still alive after I'
	R
	'take out Stessel, please place'
	R
	'me at the lowest level of the'
	R
	'army, at least...'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_02525:
	ZH 1:
	'Aristoles’s eyes were'
	R
	'unimaginably fierce next to'
	R
	'his calm, handsome face...'
	R
	'They were full of bloodlust.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_02499:
	ZH 1:
	'Hmm, interesting guy.'
	R
	'Guess he really likes Sheila.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_0247d:
	ZH 1:
	'Fine.'
	R
	'I’ll do that.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'Thank you.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Um...'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_0247d:
	ZH 1:
	'What, is there more?'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'No...'
	R
	'May I be excused?'
	R
	'...It’s time for Sheila’s'
	R
	'medication.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_0247d:
	ZH 1:
	'Yeah, you’re excused.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'Thank you.'
	R
	'Goodbye, then...'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_02525:
	ZH 1:
	'Aristoles stood up gracefully'
	R
	'and left Rance’s sight.'
