	\L_024d1:
	\L_024b5:
	ZH 1:
	'　Planned City Laurengrad'
	R
	R
	'  2nd Army HQ - Rear Garden'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'2nd Army General Aristoles was'
	R
	'in the beautifully maintained'
	R
	'garden, lost in thought.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_02499:
	ZH 1:
	'War with Leazas...?'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'...Patton...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'It was years ago...'
	R
	'My friend took down Leazas,'
	R
	'then got counterattacked and'
	R
	'went missing...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Ridiculous... I gave up back'
	R
	'then, but this stinks of'
	R
	'conspiracy...'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024b5:
	ZH 1:
	'Aristoles looked up at the'
	R
	'deep blue sky.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_02499:
	ZH 1:
	'............'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Empress Sheila... Are the'
	R
	'rumors that you hate him true?'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'You, who always looked at your'
	R
	'brother-in-law Patton with'
	R
	'worry at banquets and so many'
	R
	'public gatherings...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'I don’t want to believe you'
	R
	'would give orders to have'
	R
	'Patton killed...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Dowager Empress Pamela and'
	R
	'that pale man... Stessel...'
	R
	'are likely pulling the strings,'
	R
	'but...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'I’ve yet to even get proof of'
	R
	'that. If I could just get some'
	R
	'somehow...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'I keep sending out spies to'
	R
	'get any... But I still haven’t'
	R
	'obtained any significant'
	R
	'information...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Impressive, Stessel... You may'
	R
	'be an enemy, but I acknowledge'
	R
	'your intelligence... I can’t'
	R
	'respect you, though...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'If Pamela and Stessel are'
	R
	'found as the puppet masters,'
	R
	'maybe banishment, or... They'
	R
	'likely can’t escape execution.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'And then... Empress Sheila'
	R
	'will be left, and I should be'
	R
	'able to protect her if I take'
	R
	'her in.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Then... In the off chance that'
	R
	'Patton happens to be alive and'
	R
	'he returns to this country...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'I want to believe everything'
	R
	'will go well...'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024b5:
	ZH 1:
	'The opportunity for Patton and'
	R
	'Aristoles to meet was given by'
	R
	'Thoma, who was now dead.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Aristoles was twelve back then.'
	R
	'Patton was ten.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Aristoles was already treated'
	R
	'as a prodigy, and received'
	R
	'respect, fear, and jealousy as'
	R
	'a crossbow master.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'At a time when he was'
	R
	'overwhelmed by trying to be'
	R
	'perfect at everything, he met'
	R
	'Thoma, and then...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Thoma had said he wanted to'
	R
	'introduce him to someone, so'
	R
	'he followed passively to meet'
	R
	'Patton, rude but training hard.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Their personalities and'
	R
	'characters were complete'
	R
	'opposites.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'But, perhaps because of that,'
	R
	'they became friends in no time'
	R
	'at all.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'That was 20 years ago.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_02499:
	ZH 1:
	'Patton...'
	R
	'Where are you now and what are'
	R
	'you doing?'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Are you really dead like the'
	R
	'rumors say? Do you live?'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'Aaaaaagh, geez!'
	R
	'What’re you doin’ here,'
	R
	'General Aristoles!?'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	!VAR0516 : 433!
	\L_02541:
	\L_02525:
	ZH 1:
	'The fat man that ran like he'
	R
	'was dragging himself was'
	R
	'Aristoles’s subordinate,'
	R
	'Convert Tax.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'What’re you loiterin’ around'
	R
	'here for?!'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'We’re at war!'
	R
	'Mr. Stessel’s gonna yell at us'
	R
	'if we don’t go out and fight.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_0247d:
	ZH 1:
	'............'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Hmph...'
	R
	'What do I care?'
	R
	'I have no intention of'
	R
	'fighting for him.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_02509:
	ZH 1:
	'...Ack... That was a mistake.'
	R
	'Can’t say Mr. Stessel’s name'
	R
	'around this guy.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Since he suspects it was Mr.'
	R
	'Stessel that drove Prince'
	R
	'Patton out...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Well, guess anyone’d feel bad'
	R
	'if their good friend was'
	R
	'killed...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Can’t say that, though.'
	R
	'Mr. Stessel told me to use'
	R
	'him...'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'Aah, right.'
	R
	'On a different subject...'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_0247d:
	ZH 1:
	'What?'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'A letter came for you from'
	R
	'Empress Sheila. Look.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_0247d:
	ZH 1:
	'What!?'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024b5:
	ZH 1:
	'Aristoles snatched the letter'
	R
	'from Convert’s hands.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'  To my beloved Aristoles.'
	R
	'  How are you?'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'  As I live like a caged bird'
	R
	'  in this castle, I can only'
	R
	'  know what you’re doing via'
	R
	'  reports on paper.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'  I’m lonely. While their'
	R
	'  army’s not as great as ours,'
	R
	'  the Leazas Army is strong...'
	R
	'  I believe they’re a problem.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'  But Aristoles...'
	R
	'  For our citizens who are'
	R
	'  forced to live lives of'
	R
	'  poverty...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'　　And for me, please fight...'
	R
	'  Please protect us...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'  I will be sincerely waiting'
	R
	'  for reports from you in the'
	R
	'  castle.'
	R
	'            Sheila'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_0247d:
	ZH 1:
	'Empress Sheila...'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024b5:
	ZH 1:
	'Aristoles hugged the letter'
	R
	'against his chest like he was'
	R
	'in love with it.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'What’d it say?'
	R
	'A letter directly from Empress'
	R
	'Sheila...'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_0247d:
	ZH 1:
	'Don’t touch it.'
	R
	'This letter was written for me'
	R
	'alone.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Nobody else can look at it, or'
	R
	'even touch it.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'Huh... Sorry...'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_02499:
	ZH 1:
	'Empress Sheila...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Yes... The reason I stay in'
	R
	'this country isn’t for the'
	R
	'people, for Pamela...'
	R
	'And certainly not for Stessel.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Empress Sheila. For you alone,'
	R
	'I’d even listen to the orders'
	R
	'of the man who killed my'
	R
	'friend... And give my life.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Yes...'
	R
	'So I will stay here rather'
	R
	'than leave the country and'
	R
	'look for Patton...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'For you alone...'
	R
	'If it’s for you, I could do'
	R
	'anything...'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_0247d:
	ZH 1:
	'Convert.'
	R
	'Tell the whole army to prepare'
	R
	'to depart.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'Sure, you got it.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_02525:
	ZH 1:
	'Convert lumbered away.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024df:
	\L_02509:
	ZH 1:
	'He sure is weak to Empress'
	R
	'Sheila...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'I’m told Mr. Stessel ordered'
	R
	'Empress Sheila to write that'
	R
	'letter, but...'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Guess he doesn’t know that.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Guy’s normally frightfully'
	R
	'clear-headed, but when it'
	R
	'comes to Empress Sheila, he’s'
	R
	'completely... defenseless.'
	\L_025a2:
	ZH 1:
	'Well, thanks to that I can use'
	R
	'him too.'
	R
	'Thanks, Empress Sheila.'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_024ed:
	ZH 1:
	'Everyone～～!'
	R
	'Prepare to depart～～～!'
	\L_025a2:
	\L_02595:
	\L_02525:
	ZH 1:
	'Convert grinned as he shouted.'
